course: dictionary
lesson: 886
title: What is a biome?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A biome is a large region of the Earth with its own climate, plants and animals. «A biome is a large region with its own climate, plants and animals.» Climate means the usual weather of a place over many years. So a biome is a big area where the weather, plants and animals all belong together.
explain: Read the words around the new word for clues. The sentence says a biome is large, so it is not one tree, one pond or one garden. It is a whole region of the Earth.
explain: «Rainforests have more kinds of plants and animals than any other land biome.» Here a rainforest is one kind of biome, and it has more kinds of living things than the others. Ask yourself: what word would fit in place of biome? A large area with its own nature fits, so you are on the right track.
explain: Which biome a place has depends mostly on how warm it is and how much rain falls there. Hot, wet places have rainforests. Cold places have tundra. Your own area has a biome too, even if you have never thought about it.
fact: A biome is a large region of the Earth with its own climate, plants and animals.
fact: Climate means the usual weather of a place over many years.
fact: Main land biomes include tropical rainforest, desert, grassland (savanna), temperate forest, taiga and tundra.
fact: The plants and animals in each biome are adapted to its temperature and rainfall, which means they are suited to living there.
fact: «Rainforests» have more kinds of plants and animals than any other land biome, arranged in layers from the dark forest floor up to the canopy of leaves.
exercise: «A biome is a large region with its own climate, plants and animals.» What is a biome? | A kind of animal | A single tree in a park | *A large area of the Earth with its own climate, plants and animals | A type of weather, like rain
exercise: «Rainforests have more kinds of plants and animals than any other land biome.» Which biome has the most kinds of living things? | Grassland | *Rainforest | Tundra | Desert
exercise: Which biome a place has depends mostly on what? | How tall the buildings are | *How warm it is and how much rain falls there | What time of day it is | Which sports the people play
test: Which of these is a biome? | A library | A bicycle | *A desert | A birthday party
test: What does climate mean? | A very loud noise | A type of plant | A kind of food | *The usual weather of a place over many years
exam: «The tundra and the desert are different biomes.» Why are they different biomes? | *Because they have different climates, plants and animals | Because they are both hot and sandy | Because they are both found inside cities | Because they are both very small areas
